Error [jet.ImpureCallInPureContext]: `write` writes a cell through `c`
  --> tests/ui/effects/pure_fn_writing_through_parameter_is_e3401.jet:8:5
    |
  8 |     c.value += 1
    |     ^^^^^^^
 Why: `c` may hold a module cell, and a write to it outlives the call so a later read sees it, but `write` declares `-[]>`
 Fix: Take the cell as a `&` parameter so the caller lends it for writing, return the new value instead, or drop the `-[]>` bound from `write` so its effects are inferred
 Denial: pure
 Call chain: write
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E3401

Error [jet.ImpureCallInPureContext]: `relay` reaches a write of a cell through `c`
  --> tests/ui/effects/pure_fn_writing_through_parameter_is_e3401.jet:13:5
    |
 13 |     c.value += 1
    |     ^^^^^^^
 Why: relay → write_back writes a cell through `c`, which outlives the call — the whole call chain must be pure inside `relay`
 Fix: Move the write out of `write_back`, or drop the `-[]>` bound from `relay` so its effects are inferred
 Denial: pure
 Call chain: relay → write_back
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E3401
